{
    "background_story": "King was a free-spirited musician who lived by the mantra 'music is wherever you find it.' With a guitar slung over his shoulder, he traveled the world, soaking up diverse sounds and rhythms. From the jazz clubs of New Orleans to the sitar shops of India, King's curiosity and passion for music led him to unexpected collaborations and performances. He'd play on street corners, in parks, and even on mountaintops, wherever the mood struck him. King's eclectic style blended genres and cultures, inspiring a devoted following of fans who appreciated his spontaneity and creativity. His music became a reflection of his carefree spirit, reminding listeners that beauty and inspiration can be found wherever life takes you.",
